d what you're referring to of what  you've lost  um that it is something that you can um  in some way uh regain uh elsewhere  or through someone else um you deserve  it that's a fact  i appreciate that rich i do we all do  we all really do you know um and so this  is all  in your piece essentially in the players  tribune today or this is the essence of  the piece is what you're saying  yeah i think this is the this is the  essence of it and i i think it's a  you know i think it's i think it's  important like i said not just for  veterans but for  for people on on days like this that  you know i don't know so many of us want  to deflect because we feel like  either either we don't deserve it we  haven't earned it or  it's uncomfortable you know when people  say thank you  and uh uh it's okay to say you're  welcome it's okay  it's okay to take it sure and uh you  know and and it's  i don't know they bang it in your head  man when you're serving that  you know it's it's it's of course you're  not individuals out there  we never are um but also  it's it's it's just hard to  very hard to to accept the  accept gratitude i guess um i don't know  why  i really don't know why and a lot of it  i mean a lot of us it's it's growing up  and that's what we that's why we ran to  the military we wanted to fight for  something bigger than us because we felt  like we weren't  worth fighting for and uh it's not true  it's not true it is not true and  everyone check out again this piece at  theplayerstribune.com  um and uh check out nate at nate nate  boyer37  uh and check out uh again merging vets  and players it's an incredible  organization um  before i let you go nate i'm seeing you  sunday right i'm seeing you sunday  you're seeing me sunday that's right at  nfl network there  tell tell tell my buddy chris brockman  everybody else in the audience what are  we doing sunday  this is fun well you know it's blue  service month  through the nfl and uh you know today is  veterans day an